Leave-one-out cross-validation
Leaveone -out cross-validation ( LOOCV ) is a particular  case  of  leavep -out  cross-validation  with p = 1.  The process looks similar to jackknife; however, with cross-validation one computes a statistic on the left-out sample(s), while with jackknifing  one  computes  a  statistic  from  the  kept samples only.
